From 1ca5448170897fa7ed6a3c59974b720439e72592 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre-Hugues Husson <phh@phh.me>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:06:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] board: qualcomm: add the F(x)tec Pro1 dev second stage

Add the board data for the MSM8998 F(x)tec Pro1 (QX1000).  The shared
MSM8998 DTS already describes the phone, so the U-Boot overlay only
needs the pieces the harness uses:

  - the ABL framebuffer at 0x9d600000, 1080x2160, without clock or
    power-domain phandles;
  - the BLSP2 UART at 19.2 MHz, because the GCC is a stub;
  - USB2 peripheral only, dropping the USB3 PHY that has no driver;
  - a 128 KiB 2ndstage log at 0xffd00000, after the 1 MiB ramoops at
    0xffc00000;
  - storage, PCIe, WiFi, Bluetooth and touch disabled.

The USB glue node's GCC power-domain and reset references are removed:
the GCC is a clock stub, so those providers do not exist and the DWC3
wrapper aborts when the reset lookup fails.  ABL leaves the controller
powered and out of reset.

The board file pins the fastboot buffer at 0xa0000000 below 4 GiB and
reserves it in LMB.  It also stops U-Boot below the reserved windows so
the previous boot's pstore and its own log survive, and makes
LMB_LIMIT_DMA_BELOW_RAM_TOP default for Snapdragon so bootm keeps the
kernel below the same line.

Nothing here has been run on a Pro1.
---
